Bound the baseline span of a TextPool.

TextPool::addWord() grows its bucket vector (one bucket per 4 px of baseline)
until it covers every word's baseline. A word whose baseline lies far away from
the others therefore sizes the pool from file values alone: here
"1000000 -100 0 792 792 -1 cm" with a 5 Tf font gives chars whose advance
(~5e12 px) reaches into the page, so they pass TextPage::addChar()'s page bounds
check, but whose origins sit at y = -2.45e8 and -9.5e7. The two words need a
37.5M-bucket pool: 300 MB on wasm32 (bad_alloc there, after vector growth),
600 MB on 64-bit; baselines near the INT_MAX/4 bucket limit would need up to
2^32 buckets (64 GB). Cap the pool at 2^20 buckets (a 4M px baseline span;
real pages need a few thousand) and drop words that would exceed it, like the
existing "wordBaseIdx out of range" check does. Also grow in one step instead
of 128 buckets per insert(), which was quadratic for pool.begin().

Regression test cpp/tests/poppler-textpool-baseline-test.cpp extracts the text
of a page with two words ~1.8e8 px of baseline apart and fails every operator
new above 256 MB.

Not fixed upstream as of d828315.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for TextPool,
addWord, TextOutputDev).

